Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.50,-1:59:59.60,Title,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,465)}H009  
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.50,-1:59:59.60,TitleJa,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,575)}日曜日のピクニック
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.00,0:01:02.22,Header,,0,0,0,,H009  •  時・条件の副詞節では、未来も現在形
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.00,0:00:04.10,English,,0,0,0,,I was discussing the Sunday picnic with my sister.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:04.10,0:00:10.24,English,,0,0,0,,If the weather is good, we will spend the day in a meadow by the river.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:10.24,0:00:15.02,English,,0,0,0,,If it rains, we will watch a movie at home.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:15.02,0:00:18.58,English,,0,0,0,,Unless it rains, we will leave the house at ten in the morning.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:18.58,0:00:22.70,English,,0,0,0,,We thought about several conditions and made a clear plan.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:22.70,0:00:28.92,English,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow morning, unless the forecast turns much worse, we will go as planned.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:28.92,0:00:33.40,English,,0,0,0,,If it does rain, however, we will shift the picnic to the afternoon.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:33.40,0:00:38.24,English,,0,0,0,,Whenever the forecast improves, our spirits rise with it.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:38.24,0:00:42.60,English,,0,0,0,,Mother was tired, but she said she would prepare sandwiches.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:42.60,0:00:48.06,English,,0,0,0,,The sight of sandwiches filling an entire basket is always a pleasant one.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:48.90,0:00:54.36,English,,0,0,0,,As Sunday approaches, my sister's face remains calm.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:54.36,0:01:02.02,English,,0,0,0,,The fact that everything would depend on the weather brought our family quietly together.
